---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { people } from "../lib/people.js";
import crossings from "../data/crossings.json";
import burials from "../data/burials.json";
import additions from "../data/additions.json";

/* The Crupi arrived through a marriage rather than a descent, so they fall
   outside the four-quarters story and had no place on the site at all — six
   people documented across two countries and visible only as rows in a table.
   They are here because Brisbane is where they actually are. */
const crupi = additions.filter((a) => /\bCrupi\b/.test(a.name));
const here = people.filter((p) => !p.living && [p.birthPlace, p.deathPlace, p.burialPlace]
  .some((x) => (x || "").includes("Queensland")));
const au = crossings.filter((c) => /Fremantle|Brisbane/.test(c.arrived));
---
<Base title="Brisbane" eyebrow="Queensland"
      dek="Where four families from three towns became one. Every arrival in this archive after the Second World War came through Genoa, and every one of them landed at Fremantle or Brisbane between 1949 and 1957.">

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{au.length}</div><div class="l">recorded arrivals in Australia</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">1925</div><div class="l">the first of them, and he did not survive the year after</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{burials.filter((b) => b.place.includes("Nudgee")).length}</div><div class="l">buried at <a href={u("/nudgee/")} style="color:inherit">Nudgee</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>The first one out</h2>
    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:.8rem"><P n="Michele Mazza" bold={true} /> was born at Catania in
    1909 and landed at <strong>Fremantle on 21 April 1925</strong>, aged about sixteen. He died in
    <strong>Queensland the following year</strong>. He is the earliest Australian arrival in this
    archive and the shortest life in it, and he came out a full twenty-four years before the family
    that followed him.</p>
    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:1rem">Whether he was the reason the others chose Queensland —
    whether there was already a Mazza name at an address in Brisbane when
    <P n="Sebastiano Mazza" /> stepped off at Fremantle in 1949 — is not something the archive can
    presently answer. It is a good question and it is written down.
    <a href={u("/open-questions/")}>Open questions →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>The post-war arrivals</h2>
    <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:16px">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th class="m">Born</th><th>Left</th><th>Arrived</th><th class="m">Date</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {au.map((c) => (
            <tr><td><a href={u("/people/" + c.slug)}>{c.who}</a></td>
                <td class="m">{c.born || ""}</td>
                <td>{c.left || "—"}</td><td>{c.arrived}</td>
                <td class="m">{c.arrivedDate}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">Fremantle was the first Australian landfall for ships out of the Suez route; a
    Brisbane-bound migrant was frequently disembarked and recorded there, then continued east.
    A Fremantle arrival in this table is not evidence that the person settled in Western Australia.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">A family that arrived sideways</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">The Crupi, who came through a marriage</h2>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>The family tree has one of them, and it has her name wrong. <strong>“Angela Cupo”</strong> is
      <strong>ANGELA CRUPI</strong>, born 20 December 1900, who married Rosario Mazza and lies at Nudgee.
      Her Queensland death registration of 1973 names her parents — <strong>Francesco Crupi</strong> and
      <strong>Maria Vecchio</strong> — and the same two names appear on three more registrations.</p>
      <p><strong>She had brothers here, and nobody knew.</strong> Pietro, Antonino and Mario Crupi all
      died in Queensland and all three registrations give the same parents as hers. Two of them —
      <strong>Pietro and Antonino</strong> — came into Brisbane together on the <strong>OTRANTO on 19
      August 1930</strong>, consecutive entries in the Brisbane aliens register. Angela followed on the
      <strong>VIMINALE on 7 December 1937</strong> with two daughters, aged fifteen and eight — an arrival
      this archive had no record of at all.</p>
      <p><strong>Antonino was interned.</strong> His aliens card is stamped <strong>LOVEDAY 35924</strong>;
      the reverse records him moved <em>“ex Gaythorne to 14A”</em> on 16 March 1943 and released back to
      Queensland on 22 October 1943. He was a boot repairer at Ingham, five feet four, black eyes, black
      hair, <em>the fourth finger of his right hand deformed</em> — and born at
      <strong>Piedimonte Etneo</strong>, the Mazza's own town.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>And one absence turned out to have a reason.</strong> Pietro has no aliens
      registration card, which looked like a gap. <em>NAA: BP4/3, ITALIAN CRUPI P</em> records
      “Alien Registration Certificate <strong>NOT ISSUED</strong>”, the folio noting that he was
      <strong>naturalised on 23 February 1932</strong>. By 1939 he was a British subject and outside the
      series. An explained absence and an unexplained one look identical until somebody checks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rec" style="margin-top:20px">
      {crupi.map((c) => (
        <>
          <div class="k">{c.born && c.born !== "—" ? c.born : "no date"}</div>
          <div class="v"><strong>{c.name}</strong> — {c.note}</div>
          <div class="w"></div>
        </>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>Everyone the archive places in Queensland</h2>
    <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:16px">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th class="m">Dates</th><th>Born</th><th>Died</th><th>Buried</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {here.sort((a, b) => (a.born || 9999) - (b.born || 9999)).map((p) => (
            <tr><td><a href={u("/people/" + p.slug)}>{p.name}</a></td>
                <td class="m">{[p.born, p.died].filter(Boolean).join("–")}</td>
                <td>{p.birthPlace}</td><td>{p.deathPlace}</td><td>{p.burialPlace}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
